<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malebo Pool</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Stanley Pool</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malebo Pool, formerly Stanley Pool, is a wide, lake-like stretch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a> about 35 kilometres long, just above the rapids that block navigation to the sea. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinshasa">Kinshasa</a> lies on its southern shore and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazzaville">Brazzaville</a> on its northern, making it the meeting point of river traffic from the interior. The Tio kingdom held the plateaus to its north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malebo-pool.jpg" alt="Malebo Pool" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinshasa_%26_Brazzaville_-_ISS007-E-6305.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
